<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Edward Stuart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1720–1788</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Bonnie Prince Charlie, the Young Pretender</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Edward Stuart, known as Bonnie Prince Charlie or the Young Pretender, was the elder son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-francis-edward-stuart">James Francis Edward Stuart</a> and the Jacobite claimant to the British throne. In 1745 he landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, raised the Highland clans, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> and advanced to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derby">Derby</a> before retreating. After defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-culloden">Culloden</a> in 1746 he escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and spent the rest of his life in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-edward-stuart.jpg" alt="Charles Edward Stuart" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Allan Ramsay · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lost_Portrait_of_Charles_Edward_Stuart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
